---
title: Branzino almondine
tags: [weekend]
source: Branzino Almondine by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/branzino-almondine
---

> A restaurant recipe: the olive conserva and the crema make enough for many plates; the assembly is for one fillet.

== Olive conserva ==

Warm the @extra virgin olive oil{60%ml} in a #rondeau{} over medium heat. Add the @fennel{360%g}(diced) and @lemon peel{30%g}(finely diced) and cook gently until translucent.

Add the @raisins{310%g}(sultanas), @dried currants{100%g}, @capers{90%g}(chopped), @verjus{135%ml}(white) and @Champagne vinegar{120%ml}. Turn the heat down and cook until the liquid is almost gone.

Take off the heat and add the @lemon juice{80%ml}. Fold in the @Castelvetrano olives{230%g}(halved), @thyme{1/2%bunch}(leaves only) and @lemon oil{35%ml}. Season with @kosher salt{} and refrigerate.

== Brown butter crema ==

Bring the @whole milk{480%g}, @heavy cream{150%g}, @thyme{1/2%bunch}(leaves only) and @bay leaf{1} to a simmer in a #saucepan{}.

Blend with the @milk powder{150%g}(toasted) and @butter{70%g}(browned) in a #blender{} until smooth. Season with @kosher salt{}, sieve, and keep warm over low heat.

== Assembly ==

Sear the @branzino{1}(fillet) in a #sauté pan{} over medium-high heat until done to your liking.

Toss some of the conserva with @almonds{}(Marcona, roasted), a little @lemon oil{}, and chopped @dill{}, @parsley{} and @chives{}.

Spoon crema onto the plate, set the fish on it and spoon the conserva alongside. Finish with @Meyer lemon{1}(halved, grilled) and @watercress{}(red).
